comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-04T06:03:51.696Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: the published dependency range remains @types/node >=22 while the development constraint is ^26.4.1 and the lockfile resolves a single 26.4.1 instance across Vite/Vitest. Complete repository/package/example typecheck passes. Live pnpm outdated now contains only npm-package-arg 14 (pm-ksr40d) and TypeScript 7 (pm-do5b); pnpm audit reports zero vulnerabilities across 424 dependencies and GitHub dependency/code/secret alert inventories are all zero."
  "2026-09-04T06:23:34.543Z","harness:codex","Final repository verification: pnpm quality:static passed the complete mandatory static gate; node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage passed 603 files and 8,350 tests at exact 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines; pnpm security:scan, pnpm audit, documentation links, and package-artifact checks passed. GitHub Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning alert inventories were empty. TypeScript validation passed with @types/node 26.4.1, pnpm audit reports zero vulnerabilities, and pnpm outdated leaves only the already-tracked engine-incompatible npm-package-arg 14 and TypeScript 7 migrations."
  "2026-09-04T06:42:50.470Z","harness:codex","Terminal closeout evidence: exact-tree coverage passed 603 files and 8,351 tests at 100/100/100/100; full static quality and the packed npx/bunx acceptance passed with the compatible Node type patch present in the workspace."
  "2026-09-04T08:20:00.150Z","harness:codex","Dependency/security evidence refreshed for the remediation head: GitHub reports zero open Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning alerts; repository secret scan passed. The npm advisory endpoint timed out after bounded retries and will be retried before merge rather than treated as a clean result."
  "2026-09-04T08:27:54.938Z","harness:codex","Registry advisory retry completed successfully: pnpm audit --audit-level=low reported no known vulnerabilities. This complements the zero-open Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning inventories and the repository secret scan."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-04T06:22:43.791Z","harness:codex","When the same package appears in runtime and development dependencies, pnpm update can rewrite the published compatibility range; inspect and restore the manifest range before regenerating the lockfile."
